  "title": "Tree-like Res(xor) size is bounded by F2 polynomial-calculus degree",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "If a parity decision tree with s leaves solves a width-w CNF's false-clause search, the CNF has an F2 polynomial-calculus refutation of degree at most log2 s + w (Ben-Sasson-Wigderson's induction with linear queries); so tree-like Res(xor) refutations of the sphere's count have size at least 2^(deg_PC - 3), and a size lower bound follows from an F2 polynomial-calculus degree lower bound.",
